Hi Stijn,

Those speed and distance estimates should decrease with increasing location error. This was due to a bad integral approximation being made for the error-ellipse calculations in that function - the exact integrals cannot be computed in closed form. I redid the integral approximation in a way that makes sense and should always behave correctly. The update is on GitHub.

To answer your first question, you could use the lower-limit of the CI instead of the point estimate to threshold for outliers.

Best,
Chris

