Hi Ismael,

The true mean speed of the model is speed(mov.mod1) .

Method 1 is the true Gaussian RMS speed, which is proportional to the mean speed, but not exactly the same.
Method 2 is Method 1 + statistical noise and bias from estimation.
Method 3 should give you the truth on average.
Method 4 is the best estimate of the mean speed if you didn't have velocity information, but will still have some statistical noise and bias with finite sampling.

https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s40462-019-0177-1

Best,
Chris

