Hi Stijn,

The CIs also include the error dependence, if that is what you are asking. You could probably always use the lower limit of the CI, but that involves deciding on the coverage probability.

Asymptotically, CIs are normal, so it would be the usual mean - 1.96*SE for the lower limit of the 95% CI. I need to export the fancier CI functions that assume different sampling distributions, which can be more suitable with boundary conditions, but, asymptotically, they are all the same. I've put that on my to-do list.

Best,
Chris

